  "settings/tournament": {
    "name": "The 5-Variant Chess Gauntlet (6 Clubs)",
    "winPoints": 2,
    "drawPoints": 1,
    "lossPoints": 0,
    "autoConfirm": true,
    "conditions": "### The 5-Variant Chess Gauntlet\nWelcome to the Inter-Club Chess Championship! Instead of standard slow chess, 6 clubs (T1–T6) compete simultaneously across 5 fast-paced rounds, facing every other club once—and playing a different chess variant in every single round.\n\n#### Tournament Format & Scoring\n- **Structure:** 5-Round Rotating League (3 matches played simultaneously per round).\n- **Time Control:** 10 minutes per player (10 min) across all rounds.\n- **Rest Breaks:** 3–4 minutes between Rounds 1–4, and a 5-minute break before the Round 5 finale.\n- **Points System:**\n  - 👑 **Win:** 2 Points\n  - 🤝 **Draw:** 1 Point\n  - ❌ **Loss:** 0 Points\n- **Tie-Breakers:** If clubs finish tied on points after Round 5, rankings are decided by **Head-to-Head result**, followed by **Total Wins**.\n\n#### The 5 Variants (Round by Round)\n- **Round 1 — Classic (10 min):** Standard chess rules at 10 minutes per player. Checkmate or run your opponent out of time to win.\n- **Round 2 — Duck Chess:** Played with a physical \"Duck\" token on the board. On every turn, make a normal move and then place the Duck on any empty square. Neither player can move through or land on the Duck. **Win Condition:** Capture the opponent's King (or stalemate = WIN for trapped player).\n- **Round 3 — Giveaway Chess (Anti-Chess):** Everything is reversed: your goal is to lose all of your pieces (or get stalemated). **Win Condition:** Capturing is mandatory. Kings have no special value.\n- **Round 4 — 3-Check Chess:** Played with 3 check tokens per player. **Win Condition:** First to put opponent's King in check 3 times (regular checkmate also wins). Must announce \"Check\" out loud; false check call results in +1 minute penalty.\n- **Round 5 — Physical Relay Chess (The Finale):** Standard chess rules with a physical twist: when in Check, the checked player cannot touch any chess piece until they sprint to their designated marker, grab the ball, and return it to the table cup. **Win Condition:** Checkmate or win on the clock.\n\n#### Matchup Schedule\n- **Round 1 (Classic 10 min):** Match 1: T1 vs T6 | Match 2: T2 vs T5 | Match 3: T3 vs T4\n- **Round 2 (Duck Chess):** Match 1: T5 vs T3 | Match 2: T1 vs T2 | Match 3: T6 vs T4\n- **Round 3 (Giveaway Chess):** Match 1: T4 vs T2 | Match 2: T5 vs T6 | Match 3: T3 vs T1\n- **Round 4 (3-Check Chess):** Match 1: T2 vs T6 | Match 2: T1 vs T4 | Match 3: T3 vs T5\n- **Round 5 (Physical Relay Chess):** Match 1: T1 vs T5 | Match 2: T6 vs T3 | Match 3: T4 vs T2",
    "announcement": "Welcome to the 5-Variant Chess Gauntlet! Check the Conditions tab for the 5 variants and round schedules.",
    "updatedAt": 1795198514521
  },
